<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sajjan Singh of Ratlam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sajjan Singh was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> maharaja of Ratlam, a princely state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, from 1893 until 1947. Under British paramountcy he ruled a salute state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa-agency">Malwa Agency</a>, and he served as an officer with the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-army">Indian Army</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. Shortly after his death Ratlam joined the union of Madhya Bharat in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sajjan-singh-of-ratlam.jpg" alt="Sajjan Singh of Ratlam" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raoul Hideux · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_portrait_of_Maharaja_Sajjan_Singh_of_Ratlam_(by_Raoul_Hideux)_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
